##
#
# Supersonic channel flow past a cylinder in 2D at Mach 3, Figure 1 of [1].
#
# The geometry is a disc of diameter 0.5 positioned at coordinates {0.6,0}
# in a channel [0,4] x [-1,1]. The channel is initially filled with a
# uniform flow at Mach 3 (rho = 1.4, v = 3, p = 1, gamma = 1.4). On the
# left inflow boundary Dirichlet boundary conditions and on the right
# outflow boundary "do nothing" conditions are enforced. On all other
# boundaries (top and bottom boundary of the channel and the cylinder
# boundary) slip boundary conditions are enforced.
#
# Warning, this is a large computation!
#
# The chosen refinement level 10 corresponds to around 38M gridpoints (151M
# degrees of freedom) as in Figure 1 of [1], which shows a Schlieren plot
# at t = 3.5. Every refinement level increases the number of gridpoints by
# 4 and the number of time steps by 2. Refinement level 8 (2.36M gridpoints
# already shows the same flow features and is 64 times cheaper.
#
# Note: The same configuration, shifted to the domain [0,4] x [0,2], is
# shown in Section 5.7, Figure 3 of [2]; those results were computed with
# P1 elements on an unstructured mesh with 252820 nodes and CFL 0.3 by a
# code different from ryujin.
#
# The final time is set to t = 3.5 and we output a vtk every δt = 0.1. For
# postprocessing the simulation into a nice video set the output frequency
# to δt = 0.01 which will result in a 25.0 seconds long video at 20 fps.
#
# [1] M. Maier, M. Kronbichler. Efficient parallel 3D computation of the
#     compressible Euler equations with an invariant-domain preserving
#     second-order finite-element scheme. ACM Trans. Parallel Comput.,
#     8(3):16:1-30, 2021. DOI 10.1145/3470637, arXiv:2007.00094
#
# [2] J.-L. Guermond, M. Nazarov, B. Popov, I. Tomas. Second-order
#     invariant domain preserving approximation of the Euler equations
#     using convex limiting. SIAM J. Sci. Comput., 40(5):A3211-A3239, 2018.
#     DOI 10.1137/17M1149961
#
##

subsection A - Scheduler
  set basename          = mach3-cylinder-2d

  set tasks             = vtu output

  set final time        = 5.00
  set timer granularity = 0.10
end


subsection B - Equation
  set dimension = 2
  set equation  = euler
  set gamma     = 1.4
end


subsection C - Discretization
  set geometry            = cylinder

  set mesh refinement     = 10

  subsection cylinder
    set height          = 2
    set length          = 4
    set object diameter = 0.5
    set object position = 0.6
  end
end


subsection E - InitialValues
  set configuration = uniform

  set direction     = 1, 0
  set position      = 1, 0

  set perturbation  = 0

  subsection uniform
    set primitive state = 1.4, 3, 1
  end
end


subsection H - TimeIntegrator
  set cfl min               = 0.90
  set cfl max               = 0.90
  set cfl recovery strategy = none

  set time stepping scheme  = ssprk 33
end


subsection I - VTUOutput
  subsection full
    set use mpi io     = true
    set schlieren beta = 10
  end
end
